u dictate at the  computer and then the computer types for  you  so the kids were they were all excited  at this however  the software wouldn't recognize their  indian accent  but they had access there to english  spoken  you know in the accent that the software  would recognize  which was some kind of english accent he  came back three months later  and they were all speaking the way  those people because they were motivated  it all goes down to motivation people  will learn and his perspective is  that education is a self-organizing  system  and i mean and he has a number of  examples to prove it now  i mentioned this to my wife and she said  yeah but what about those kids that  aren't very interested  of course i mean that is the obvious  question  the those people who are interested will  learn  yeah and i think there uh  that's the big question for teachers  have more than kids but my question is  in the classroom is what they do  motivate for kids or not  and i suspect the objective because it's  more  get the curriculum through past tests  therefore they're not as concerned about  motivating  them as they could be but getting back  to languages  here are some examples rhino spike is a  community where people  on demand record like somebody would say  would you record this for me  in serbian somebody on there will record  it  and they can take it and listen to it a  lot i'll  show you we have a community called link  a lot of our members  who might be studying portuguese or  japanese  if they have texts that they want  recorded they just put them up there but  they then also  if they're let's say french speaking  they would go in there  and record stuff in french and they get  credit for doing so and so forth and so  on  uh when i show our uh  community you'll see that in our  community members  uh contribute content to la to our  library in 11 languages  and the content has to consist of text  and audio  so very often if they don't have a  native speaker  audio they will take the text that they  want get  it someone at rhino spike to record it  then they put it in our library  our members can access it for learning  french whoever uploaded that  gets points on our system for having  uploaded it  live moca is a community where people  can find friends to talk to language  exchange they record things and  native speakers critique

